  "tags": [],
  "nodes": [
    {
      "id": "2fcac03e-24ec-4ca7-9b9e-8d8b9c82c3b1",
      "name": "About this workflow",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "position": [
        -420,
        -440
      ],
      "parameters": {
        "color": 4,
        "width": 1260,
        "height": 420,
        "content": "## Research Amazon products and reviews by ASIN\n\nThis workflow retrieves current Amazon product details and recent buyer reviews for the same ASIN, then combines the two responses into one item for product research, catalog enrichment, competitive intelligence, or voice-of-customer analysis. It is designed for ecommerce teams, Amazon sellers, analysts, and developers who need structured Amazon data without maintaining browsers, proxies, or parsers.\n\n### How it works\n1. **Configure Research** stores the ASIN, marketplace, ZIP code, review page count, star filter, and sort order in one place.\n2. **Get Amazon Product** and **Get Amazon Reviews** run in parallel through Pangolinfo.\n3. **Combine Product and Reviews** joins both results for downstream storage, reporting, or AI analysis.\n\n### Setup\nThis template uses a community node and is compatible with **self-hosted n8n only**. Install `n8n-nodes-pangolinfo`, create a Pangolinfo API credential, select it on both Pangolinfo nodes, and update the fields in **Configure Research**.\n\nLearn about the [Pangolinfo Amazon Scraper API](https://www.pangolinfo.com/amazon-scraper-api/) and read the [Amazon API documentation](https://docs.pangolinfo.com/en-api-reference/amazonApi/amazonScrapeAPI)."
      },
      "typeVersion": 1
    },
    {
      "id": "62cd1c9a-c2f8-4d3e-b837-2a0a709ae46c",
      "name": "Setup instructions",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "position": [
        -40,
        460
      ],
      "parameters": {
        "color": 7,
        "width": 980,
        "height": 220,
        "content": "## Configure once, then run\n\nEdit only the values in **Configure Research** for a new product. Both API branches reuse those values. After selecting your Pangolinfo credential on the two orange nodes, click **Test workflow**.\n\nThe merged output is ready for Google Sheets, databases, BI tools, Slack alerts, or an AI analysis step."
      },
      "typeVersion": 1
    },
    {
      "id": "93d75219-2b3e-4f3c-a958-e9f5b75c9e01",
